WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Cold, dense cloud regions are favorable for collapse: gravity

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.000
can overcome thermal pressure support. Dense does not automatically

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.980
mean hot, and a bright ionized region is not

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.040
the same thing as a cold star forming core.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.780
Contraction releases gravitational energy and heats the interior. Rising

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.540
density and temperature raise gas pressure, slowing contraction. This

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.560
does not require hydrogen fusion to have started, and

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.680
interior heating does not mean surface temperature always rises

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.360
along every track. The object keeps radiating energy. Without

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.460
sustained replacement, cooling reduces pressure support and contraction resumes.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.180
Approximate force balance is different from a long term

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.800
energy balance. Luminosity may rise or fall because both

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.168
radius and surface temperature matter.
